New Features
Save reusable prompts and slash commands in ten numbered
/presets
slots, with a keyboard menu for quick access. (
#54380
,
#54381
)
Set model, reasoning effort, speed, and permission profiles directly with inline
/model
and
/permissions
arguments. (
#54378
,
#54383
)
Preview viewed and generated images in the fullscreen transcript on terminals supporting Kitty or Sixel graphics. (
#54216
)
Authenticate enterprise MCP connections using eligible Codex account grants or dedicated sign-in, including OAuth clients requiring secrets. (
#55334
,
#55859
,
#56001
)
Mask credentials during supported remote Bash commands and Zsh snapshot sessions, including credentials from custom providers. (
#54309
,
#54432
,
#56049
)
The Amazon Bedrock setup wizard is now enabled by default, with API key entry grouped alongside other AWS sign-in methods when credentials are detected. (
#56033
,
#56023
)
Bug Fixes
Failed compaction no longer leaves partial summaries in conversation history, and background compaction failures fall back without panicking. (
#53932
,
#55581
)
Resuming sessions now finds compressed histories and restores saved thread settings instead of replacing them with global defaults. (
#54008
,
#55923
)
Windows HTTPS and WebSocket connections now handle proxy authentication challenges using the signed-in user’s Negotiate or NTLM credentials. (
#55994
,
#56000
)
CLI configuration overrides are preserved when
-c
or
--config
appears at multiple subcommand levels. (
#56022
)
Queued prompts now wait for pending permission selections to resolve before continuing. (
#55682
)
Hardened sandbox checks for case-variant metadata paths on macOS and replaceable symlinks used to locate executables. (
#54273
,
#55384
)
Chores
Reduced disk usage by pruning unused installations, cleaning abandoned marketplace checkouts, and bounding daemon logs. (
#53827
,
#55149
,
#55689
,
#55690
,
#55856
)
Updated the embedded JavaScript runtime with safety checks for optimized
Array.sort
operations. (
#54519
)
